# Review: ReviewPlugin

The plugin is close to its spec and well tested. The pure lifecycle model (`deriveBinding`,
`applyViewModeSelection`) has table tests. The binding pipeline has a headless suite. The shared
scenarios run both headless (`testing/scenarios.test.tsx`) and as storybook plays
(`DocumentVersioning.stories.tsx`), which also carry the same-view swap and author-visibility plays.
The diff layer is covered by `ui-editor`'s review tests, and comment threads by the composer e2e
suite. The one real gap is F-3.2: `Branch.archiveIfEmpty` exists and is tested in
`@dxos/versioning`, but nothing calls it, so the accept and reject handlers in plugin-markdown never
archive an emptied suggestion branch. The comment operations beyond the trigger gate
(RespondToThread, delete/restore, failure notice) have no unit tests. The prohibition on comments on
suggestion branches and the shared current-change selection are untested. QA-1's resolve step is
not automated.

Of 44 items: 36 done, 6 untested, 2 partial, 0 diverged, 0 missing. (The spec's T-2 to T-8 blocks are not listed as reviewable items by `deus review items`, so they carry no verdict.)

